voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title seL4's own API compiled under our compiler -- and the boundary named by walking into it
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, advancing its study/research rungs and surfacing every gate.
think Standfast first. The REDS ledger reads with no OPEN rows -- %104, %105, %106 were closed last lap, %84, %98, %103 before them. Corrective queue genuinely empty, so constructive work may begin.
think The running thread is unambiguous across the top three logs: the license read overturned the seL4 copyleft premise, the fetch was granted and swept per file, and the newest recommend line names the next rung outright -- a close read of the capability IPC model against libsel4's own headers, which we may now link rather than study through a wall.
think The seated ordering puts the Microkernel Target ahead of Seasons A-H (Keaton's word `20260817`, double-seat doc line 101), which is exactly what REDS %104 taught. So the microkernel arc leads and the DISC crypto arc waits, and the Caravan fold queue waits with it.
think The crux inside Equinox 1 is not more prose about the capability model. The `20260821.040637` probe answered the toolchain question against OUR OWN stub because that was all the clean-room boundary allowed. The grant makes a stronger question askable for the first time: does seL4's published API itself compile under our compiler, freestanding, for riscv64.
think Measured it rather than argued it. The hand-written half of the libsel4 core compiles -- simple_types, objecttype across all three tiers, errors, constants, macros -- freestanding riscv64, e_machine 243 read from the object's own ELF header, zero dynamic NEEDED entries.
think The generated half stops at exactly one file, and that is the round's real finding. `sel4/types.h`, `syscalls.h`, `bootinfo.h`, `faults.h` and the `sel4.h` umbrella all refuse by naming `sel4/sel4_arch/types_gen.h`. Producing it wants bitfield_gen.py (imports ply); the syscall and invocation headers want jinja2. Neither module is on this pier.
think That is an environment change rather than a tree change, so it is surfaced as a named gate rather than crossed -- and made a measurement, not a note: a fixture scan prints how many of the two are missing, so a later pier that carries them reports 0 and the surface opens with no change to the witness.
think Wrote the numbers to be READ rather than recited, remembering REDS %105. The probe compiles twice -- once freestanding, once for this host beside a reporter that prints what the compiled enums actually say. A vendored bump that moves seL4's vocabulary reds this witness on the lap it lands.
think Two RED paths proven on metal before the green was trusted. Withhold our own configuration header and the compile must refuse by naming autoconf.h, which proves seL4's headers are genuinely being read. Reach past the boundary into types.h and it must refuse by naming types_gen.h, which proves the boundary is where the doc says it is.
think Re-read the right to include at the file level rather than inheriting the verdict: all six headers the probe includes carry their own BSD-2-Clause tag, none carries GPL. seL4 issue #245's shape would red this witness on the lap it returned.
think Caught one of my own claims by checking it. The design doc first named the riscv64 arch object types from memory as including an ASID pool; the headers say giga page at the mode tier, then 4K page, mega page, and page table at the arch tier. Corrected before the send -- measurement beats memory, including my own.
obs Three Rishi quoting facts learned the hard way and worth recording: a single quote inside a run string collides with the lexer, an escaped double quote does not reach the shell as a bare quote, and a space inside an escaped-quote region breaks the parse. The fix each time was a space-free unquoted grep pattern, or moving the logic into a fixture scan script where it belongs anyway.
obs The vocabulary reading is the durable half of this round. seL4 answers a capability invocation with eleven named errors; `caravan/capabilities.rye` names four outcomes. The seven that remain are a design agenda arrived at by measurement rather than by brainstorming -- delete-first and revoke-first are the derivation tree speaking, not-enough-memory is untyped retyping, truncated-message is the IPC buffer.
obs The object-type numbering composes rather than braids: generic ends at NonArchObjectTypeCount, the mode tier begins there, the arch tier begins where mode ended. One numbering, no overlap, no gap -- the same shape this tree already reaches for, arrived at independently by a formally verified kernel.
obs seL4 provides no supervision tree at all, which reframes Caravan's whole position. It is not competing with anything the kernel does; it is the thing the kernel expects someone above the line to write. The arc's Caravan-before-Tally ordering reads better for knowing that.
loom witness=microkernel_libsel4_reach headers_included=6 bsd_tagged=6 gpl_tagged=0 errors=11 objects=9 nonarch_objects=5 word_bits=64 max_prio=255 e_machine=243 dyn_needed=0 generator_modules_missing=2
file tools/microkernel_libsel4_reach_witness.rish the round's proof -- two builds, two RED paths, a per-file licence re-read, and a measured gate
file tools/fixtures/libsel4_reach_probe.c our own probe over seL4's BSD-2-Clause headers; reproduces no seL4 line, includes them
file tools/fixtures/libsel4_reach_report.c our own reporter, held apart so the probe stays libc-free
file tools/fixtures/libsel4_reach_include/autoconf.h our own minimal configuration, the two CONFIG_ macros the hand-written core reads
file tools/fixtures/libsel4_generator_deps_scan.sh the gate as a measurement -- prints how many of jinja2 and ply are missing
file external-research/20260821-043831_the-libsel4-reach-and-the-vocabulary-caravan-inherits.md the reading: what was measured, where the boundary falls, and the vocabulary mapped against Caravan's four refusals
file external-research/20260817-185851_microkernel-target-and-the-os-parity-question.md Equinox 1 addendum, in the same commit as the code it describes
file crux/REMEMBER.md Now refilled with live work -- the reached ground, the named gate, and the ungated next rung
recommend keep-going The next rung is ungated and ordinary: design Caravan's refusal mapping against the eleven in Rye, on the hosted ground it already runs on. The seven refusals Caravan cannot yet answer are the agenda, and no fetch, licence, or hardware stands between here and writing it. The one gate worth Keaton's eye is small and cheap -- jinja2 and ply on the pier's Python environment opens the rest of the libsel4 userlevel surface in a single step.
